@startuml two-wire-formats
' ============================================================================
' THE TWO WIRE FORMATS a `Par` is serialised to, and which sides were converted.
' Colour legend as in recursive-vs-trampolined.puml:
'   GREEN  #2E7D32 converted (depth-independent, measured flat)
'   AMBER  #EF6C00 still Theta(depth) native stack
'   RED    #C62828 the asymmetry: unbounded writer / bounded reader
'   PURPLE #6A1B9A wire bytes
' ============================================================================
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam defaultFontName "DejaVu Sans"
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 8
skinparam ArrowThickness 1.4
skinparam ranksep 28
skinparam nodesep 30

title <b>One term, two wire formats</b>\nonly the cold-store pair was trampolined on <i>both</i> sides

rectangle "  **`models::rhoapi::Par`**  —  the in-memory term  \n37-member recursive SCC; <latex>\{\mathtt{Par}\}</latex> is a feedback vertex set of size 1" as PAR #ECEFF1

package "**(1) COLD STORE**  —  bincode over serde, LMDB, node-local" as COLD #E8F5E9 {
  rectangle "**writer**  `bincode_encoder::encode`\nsingle-walk op-stack machine\n**CONVERTED (Stage H)**\n<latex>0</latex> B/level native" as CW #A5D6A7
  rectangle "bytes\n(non-self-describing;\nserde declaration order)" as CB #E1BEE7
  rectangle "**reader**  `bincode_decoder::cold_decode`\nobligation stack + 18 value stacks\n**CONVERTED (Stage F)**\n<latex>0</latex> B/level native" as CR #A5D6A7
  CW -[#6A1B9A,thickness=2]down-> CB
  CB -[#6A1B9A,thickness=2]down-> CR
}

package "**(2) NETWORK / CONSENSUS**  —  protobuf via `prost`" as NET #FFF3E0 {
  rectangle "**writer**  `<Par as Message>::encode_raw`\nDERIVED, recursive\n**TRIPWIRE**: gate subject `encode`\n**302 B/level** release (MEASURED)\n<b>no write-side limit</b>" as NW #FFCC80
  rectangle "bytes\n(protobuf; ascending tag order)" as NB #E1BEE7
  rectangle "**reader**  `<Par as Message>::merge_field`\nDERIVED, recursive\n**4,096 B/level** release (MEASURED)\n<b>`RECURSION_LIMIT = 100`</b>\n⇒ term depth **33 / 32 / 31** per envelope" as NR #EF9A9A
  NW -[#6A1B9A,thickness=2]down-> NB
  NB -[#6A1B9A,thickness=2]down-> NR
}

PAR -[#2E7D32,thickness=3]-> CW : cold-store write
PAR -[#EF6C00,thickness=3]-> NW : network write

note bottom of CR #E8F5E9
  **NOT in the class.**  Both directions are iterative
  and depth-unlimited, measured flat from depth 4 to
  depth 4,096 in both build profiles.  Closed by the
  codec campaign (~#46 / ~#119 / ~#121) from one
  generated table.
end note

note bottom of NR #FFEBEE
  ★★ **THE ASYMMETRY (issue ~#120).**  The writer is
  **unbounded** and the reader is **bounded**, and the
  two ends sit on different paths, processes or times.
  A term therefore exists that can be **built, reduced**
  **and serialised** and **cannot be read back**.
  Four independent instances of this one shape:
  ~#120 (the audit's §7.3) · ~#129 (`output_value`) ·
  ~#130 (the trie value slot) ·
  ~#4 (`EPathMap`'s own prost wire, tag 8)
end note

legend bottom
  |= colour |= meaning |
  |<#A5D6A7>| converted — measured <latex>0</latex> B/level |
  |<#FFCC80>| still <latex>\Theta(d)</latex>, held under a gate ceiling |
  |<#EF9A9A>| bounded reader — the refusing end of the asymmetry |
  |<#E1BEE7>| wire bytes |
endlegend

@enduml
